## Project context (mock3)

This project has two independent TypeScript codelines, both using vitest:

- **mocka** (`mock-a/`): Transit fare rules. Exports `fareFor` and `totalFor`. Ticket MOCK3-1 fixes a boundary bug where riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare instead of the concession fare — the fix should change only the age comparison operator so that 65 qualifies for the concession. When reviewing, verify the diff touches only that comparison and that a test case covering age 65 has been added or updated.
- **mockb** (`mock-b/`): Departure-board stop rendering. Exports `formatStops`. Ticket MOCK3-2 fixes a loop-bound bug where `formatStops` omits the final stop — the fix should change only the loop bound so the last stop is included. When reviewing, verify the diff touches only that bound and that a test asserting the last stop appears has been added or updated.

Both tickets are intentionally small boundary/off-by-one fixes. Large diffs or changes to unrelated files are a red flag. If an exported function's signature changes without a corresponding test update, flag it as API contract drift.

